From a1d4991371fbfffe6167e96a8e00cec131cf3f75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BOAR R&D <noreply>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:59:18 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] routing: keep number patterns linear on long digit runs

A pasted run of digits made four unanchored number patterns (the calculators' NUM, the temperature conversion, the task classifier's arithmetic test and numguard's NUM) restart at every digit, so a 20,000-digit question took seconds on a desktop and minutes on a phone before any answer. Each pattern now refuses to start inside another number ((?<!\d), and (?<!\d,) for numguard's comma-grouped form). Answers to normal questions are unchanged: full suite 1,484/1,484 with and without HEALTHGAP. Found by the native app's plugin combination suite; longDigits.test.ts fails 5/6 without this change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply>
